{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01XWvRvaUwhGzKNbgBpPu2R7", "type": "tool_result", "content": "16:A nine-part questionnaire in one message gets a three-part answer, and the six missing answers become silent assumptions. Silent assumptions are how an evaluation ends up measuring the wrong product for the wrong person.\n52:      ~90 min per persona.\n56:      ~15\u201325 min per persona, plus a crawl.\n59:      Runs (b) on the site, then (a) on the product. Two captures.\n96:Present the lenses **for the assessment type chosen**, with mode and cost \u2014 the cost is the whole point of the architecture.\n99:PRODUCT  \u00b7  Mode A \u2014 one persona traversal, scored many ways\n105:WEBSITE  \u00b7  Mode A-visit \u2014 one persona visit, scored many ways\n110:WEBSITE  \u00b7  Mode C \u2014 no session, no login\n116:WEBSITE  \u00b7  Mode B \u2014 scripted and measured, no persona\n120:WEBSITE  \u00b7  Mode D \u2014 composes the above across 2+ sites\n124:**Say the cost out loud after they choose.** Adding a lens *within a mode you are already running* is nearly free \u2014 it scores evidence already captured. Adding a *mode* means another pass. `clarity + conversion + trust` is **one** visit; `clarity + seo` is **two** captures in different modes. Users routinely assume more lenses means proportionally more time; the surprise runs the other way.\n161:If yes, per objective capture **two** things, in the user's own words:\n174:- **Captured now, before capture.** An objective the persona never pursued cannot be scored honestly afterwards.\n206:## Step 4 \u2014 Device profile per persona\n208:Ask per persona, not once for all. A persona who is mobile-dominant and one who is desktop-only are testing different products.\n272:Default: **90 minutes** per persona, with a hard stop.\n314:> Which email should the persona sign up with? I'll extend it per persona and per run \u2014 `you+novice-20260911@yourdomain` \u2014 so every run is a fresh signup. It goes in the target file as `alias_email`.\n339:Record them verbatim. Exclusions are applied at **scoring** time, not capture \u2014 the traversal still records what it sees, the analyst drops it. That distinction matters: an excluded thing that blocks the persona still explains why they got stuck.\n356:Lenses        Mode A-visit \u2192 clarity, conversion, trust\n357:              Mode C       \u2192 seo\n367:Captures      3 \u00d7 Mode A-visit traversal  (25 min cap each)\n368:              1 \u00d7 Mode C crawl            (no session)\n385:The **captures vs. scoring** split is the line that teaches the architecture. Keep it."}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "dc50efc2-8031-44dd-8e60-199c4bcb81fc", "uuid": "2124767e-442c-4175-9cb8-c14ccc1dd8b1", "timestamp": "2026-09-12T07:19:25.168Z", "tool_use_result": {"mode": "content", "numFiles": 0, "filenames": [], "content": "16:A nine-part questionnaire in one message gets a three-part answer, and the six missing answers become silent assumptions. Silent assumptions are how an evaluation ends up measuring the wrong product for the wrong person.\n52:      ~90 min per persona.\n56:      ~15\u201325 min per persona, plus a crawl.\n59:      Runs (b) on the site, then (a) on the product. Two captures.\n96:Present the lenses **for the assessment type chosen**, with mode and cost \u2014 the cost is the whole point of the architecture.\n99:PRODUCT  \u00b7  Mode A \u2014 one persona traversal, scored many ways\n105:WEBSITE  \u00b7  Mode A-visit \u2014 one persona visit, scored many ways\n110:WEBSITE  \u00b7  Mode C \u2014 no session, no login\n116:WEBSITE  \u00b7  Mode B \u2014 scripted and measured, no persona\n120:WEBSITE  \u00b7  Mode D \u2014 composes the above across 2+ sites\n124:**Say the cost out loud after they choose.** Adding a lens *within a mode you are already running* is nearly free \u2014 it scores evidence already captured. Adding a *mode* means another pass. `clarity + conversion + 