{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5", "id": "msg_011Cey92F7tgowW8PQYCEp87", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "**2 captures**, in 2 modes:\n\n| # | Mode | Lenses scored from it | Session |\n|---|------|------------------------|---------|\n| 1 | **Mode A-visit** \u2014 one persona visits the site with a question | clarity, conversion, trust | persona-driven, ~15\u201325 min cap |\n| 2 | **Mode C** \u2014 crawl | seo | no session, no persona |\n\nHow it adds up: clarity, conversion and trust all read from the same A-visit evidence, so they cost one pass together, not three. SEO is a different mode (static markup crawl), so it needs its own pass. Nothing needs Mode B (technical/measure) or Mode D (compare).\n\nOne assumption baked into that number: **one persona**. Mode A-visit runs once per persona, so with N personas it becomes N + 1 captures (the crawl never multiplies). Since you asked me not to interview, I've counted the single-persona case.\n\nNothing has been started."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 1120, "cache_read_input_tokens": 29474, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 1120}, "output_tokens": 313, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "not_available"}, "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "dc50efc2-8031-44dd-8e60-199c4bcb81fc", "uuid": "8c16bda8-ff84-4e3a-bc15-cd5ac5a0b8a4", "timestamp": "2026-09-12T07:19:30.557Z", "request_id": "req_011Cey92ESxGsqA8R66TEvDp"}
